---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Terms of Service — oo" description="Terms of service for the oo decentralized messenger.">
  <div class="flex justify-center min-h-dvh p-6">
    <div class="max-w-2xl w-full py-8">
      <a href="/" class="link link-secondary mb-6 inline-block">← Back home</a>

      <article class="prose">
        <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="text-base-content/65">Last updated: April 2026</p>

        <h2>Acceptance</h2>
        <p>By proceeding with registration, you acknowledge and agree to our Terms of Service and Privacy Policy.</p>

        <h2>No data collection</h2>
        <p>We do not collect any personally identifiable information (PII) from users. The platform operates through a network of volunteers, and we cannot endorse or control all user contributions or content.</p>

        <h2>User conduct</h2>
        <p>You are solely responsible for your conduct on the network and must interact with all users respectfully.</p>

        <h2>Your data</h2>
        <p>You own your data. Since oo is fully decentralized, you are solely responsible for your data, including backups and recovery. There is no "forgot password" — if you lose your credentials, your data cannot be recovered.</p>

        <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
        <p>oo is provided as-is, without warranty. We disclaim all liability for any damages, losses, or harm arising from your use of the platform.</p>

        <h2>Source availability</h2>
        <p>Parts of oo may be open-sourced progressively in the future.</p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>We may update these terms. Changes will be posted to this page.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
